    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166-a3">

                <pb facs="0313" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg219"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure to inclosure 2 in No.
                    135.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Black to the Burgomaster of Wurzburg.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Nuremburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">Sept. 10,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Will you be kind enough to inform me how long Mr. Seligman Rosenheim, of No. 89
                    Semmelstrasse, formerly of New York, has lived in the city of Wurzburg and its
                    vicinity? I understand that he also lived at Heidingsfeld. If so, will you be
                    kind enough to inform me also how long he lived in that place?</p>
                <p>Is he, or has he been, engaged in any business in Wurzburg, or has he always
                    lived there as a private gentleman?</p>
                <p>For any information which you can give me in regard to this subject I beg to
                    express my thanks.</p>
                <p>Yours, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. J. Black</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The letter is returned to the consulate of the United States at Nuremburg,
                        with the respectful remark that Seligman Rosenheim, born at Heidingsfeld on
                        August 17, 1821, has sojourned here as a private gentleman since 1867.</p>
                    <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">The City Magistrate</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Burgomaster.</hi></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
